<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Daehan passes on 24,000T wheat tenders.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Daehan passes on 24,000T wheat tenders.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daehan Flour Mills Co Ltd said on Friday it passed on tenders for 24,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat due to high prices.</p>
<p>A company official said shipment was set for May 15-June 15 to the western port of Inchon.  </p>
<p>Traders said the lowest bids were made by Japanese trading house Kanematsu Corp.</p>
<p>Details for the lowest bids of the passed tender are as follows:</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat		Tonne	Price/T (FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		  12,000	$156.35</p>
<p>(protein max 10.8%)</p>
<p>  Western White		1,000	$156.75</p>
<p>(club minimum 15 percent)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	    2,000	$183.05</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring     9,000	$191.25</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
